(1)  DO THE CLOSED FORMS MATCH MONTE CARLO?
================================================================================================
  M=8  R=0.45  T=4096  E0=1.7  reps=400. g known exactly.
  Both arms given the SAME readout variance here, so only sigma-resampling
  differs. Sp=1 is SPSA's best case, its largest number of perturbations.

    i      g_i     V5 emp    V5 pred   SPSA emp  SPSA pred   bias V5
  ------------------------------------------------------------------
    0   1.1013    0.00298    0.00292    0.00497    0.00462  -0.00134
    1   0.3384    0.00280    0.00318    0.00514    0.00516   0.00238
    2  -0.5400    0.00330    0.00314    0.00457    0.00507   0.00092
    3  -1.2602    0.00282    0.00282    0.00425    0.00444  -0.00196
    4  -1.8946    0.00253    0.00233    0.00321    0.00346  -0.00180
    5   0.0186    0.00292    0.00321    0.00511    0.00522   0.00428
    6  -0.8106    0.00329    0.00305    0.00525    0.00490   0.00152
    7  -0.8722    0.00311    0.00303    0.00459    0.00485  -0.00120

  If the two 'pred' columns track the two 'emp' columns, the algebra holds
